### ============================================
### Company Management API Tests
### Test full CRUD operations for companies
### ============================================

### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api
@acme_subdomain = acme
@techstart_subdomain = techstart

### ============================================
### Setup: Login to get access token
### ============================================

### 1. Login as John (Sales) in Acme
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Subdomain: {{acme_subdomain}}

{
  "email": "john.sales@tawasol.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

# @name loginAcme
### Expected: 200 OK with access token

### 2. Login as John in TechStart
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Subdomain: {{techstart_subdomain}}

{
  "email": "john.sales@techstart.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

# @name loginTechStart
### Expected: 200 OK with access token

### ============================================
### Company CRUD Operations - Acme Tenant
### ============================================

### 3. Create a new company
POST {{baseUrl}}/companies HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAcme.response.body.data.accessToken}}
X-Tenant-Subdomain: {{acme_subdomain}}

{
  "name": "TechVision Solutions",
  "industry": "Information Technology",
  "website": "https://techvision.example.com",
  "email": "info@techvision.com",
  "phone": "+1-555-1000",
  "address": "123 Tech Street",
  "city": "San Francisco",
  "state": "CA",
  "country": "USA",
  "postalCode": "94105",
  "employeeCount": 150,
  "annualRevenue": 5000000,
  "description": "Leading provider of enterprise software solutions",
  "linkedIn": "https://linkedin.com/company/techvision",
  "tags": ["enterprise", "software", "b2b"]
}

# @name createCompany1
### Expected: 201 Created with company details

### 4. Create another company (smaller)
POST {{baseUrl}}/companies HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAcme.response.body.data.accessToken}}
X-Tenant-Subdomain: {{acme_subdomain}}

{
  "name": "Green Earth Consulting",
  "industry": "Environmental Services",
  "website": "https://greenearth.example.com",
  "email": "contact@greenearth.com",
  "phone": "+1-555-2000",
  "city": "Portland",
  "state": "OR",
  "country": "USA",
  "employeeCount": 25,
  "tags": ["consulting", "sustainability"]
}

# @name createCompany2
### Expected: 201 Created

### 5. Get all companies (no filters)
GET {{baseUrl}}/companies HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAcme.response.body.data.accessToken}}
X-Tenant-Subdomain: {{acme_subdomain}}

### Expected: 200 OK with array of companies + pagination (should include seed data + new ones)

### 6. Get companies with pagination
GET {{baseUrl}}/companies?page=1&limit=10 HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAcme.response.body.data.accessToken}}
X-Tenant-Subdomain: {{acme_subdomain}}

### Expected: 200 OK with paginated results

### 7. Search companies by name
GET {{baseUrl}}/companies?search=TechVision HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAcme.response.body.data.accessToken}}
X-Tenant-Subdomain: {{acme_subdomain}}

### Expected: 200 OK with matching companies

### 8. Filter companies by industry
GET {{baseUrl}}/companies?industry=Information HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAcme.response.body.data.accessToken}}
X-Tenant-Subdomain: {{acme_subdomain}}

### Expected: 200 OK with IT companies

### 9. Filter companies by tags
GET {{baseUrl}}/companies?tags=enterprise,software HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAcme.response.body.data.accessToken}}
X-Tenant-Subdomain: {{acme_subdomain}}

### Expected: 200 OK with filtered companies

### 10. Sort companies by annual revenue (desc)
GET {{baseUrl}}/companies?sortBy=annualRevenue&sortOrder=desc HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAcme.response.body.data.accessToken}}
X-Tenant-Subdomain: {{acme_subdomain}}

### Expected: 200 OK with companies sorted by revenue

### 11. Sort companies by employee count (asc)
GET {{baseUrl}}/companies?sortBy=employeeCount&sortOrder=asc HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAcme.response.body.data.accessToken}}
X-Tenant-Subdomain: {{acme_subdomain}}

### Expected: 200 OK with companies sorted by employee count

### 12. Get a specific company by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/companies/{{createCompany1.response.body.data.id}} HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAcme.response.body.data.accessToken}}
X-Tenant-Subdomain: {{acme_subdomain}}

### Expected: 200 OK with full company details including contacts and deals

### 13. Update company
PUT {{baseUrl}}/companies/{{createCompany1.response.body.data.id}} HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAcme.response.body.data.accessToken}}
X-Tenant-Subdomain: {{acme_subdomain}}

{
  "employeeCount": 175,
  "annualRevenue": 6500000,
  "description": "Leading provider of enterprise software solutions - Recently expanded operations",
  "tags": ["enterprise", "software", "b2b", "saas"]
}

### Expected: 200 OK with updated company

### 14. Get company statistics
GET {{baseUrl}}/companies/stats HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAcme.response.body.data.accessToken}}
X-Tenant-Subdomain: {{acme_subdomain}}

### Expected: 200 OK with company statistics (total, by industry, by owner, total revenue)

### ============================================
### Tenant Isolation Tests
### ============================================

### 15. Try to access Acme company from TechStart tenant (should fail)
GET {{baseUrl}}/companies/{{createCompany1.response.body.data.id}} HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{loginTechStart.response.body.data.accessToken}}
X-Tenant-Subdomain: {{techstart_subdomain}}

### Expected: 404 Not Found (company doesn't exist in TechStart)

### 16. Create company in TechStart tenant
POST {{baseUrl}}/companies HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginTechStart.response.body.data.accessToken}}
X-Tenant-Subdomain: {{techstart_subdomain}}

{
  "name": "Digital Innovations Corp",
  "industry": "Technology",
  "website": "https://digitalinnovations.com",
  "email": "hello@digitalinnovations.com",
  "phone": "+1-555-3000",
  "city": "Seattle",
  "state": "WA",
  "country": "USA",
  "employeeCount": 75,
  "annualRevenue": 3000000,
  "tags": ["technology", "innovation"]
}

# @name createCompanyTechStart
### Expected: 201 Created (different tenant)

### 17. Verify TechStart has different companies
GET {{baseUrl}}/companies HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{loginTechStart.response.body.data.accessToken}}
X-Tenant-Subdomain: {{techstart_subdomain}}

### Expected: 200 OK with only TechStart companies (not Acme companies)

### 18. TechStart company stats (should be separate)
GET {{baseUrl}}/companies/stats HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{loginTechStart.response.body.data.accessToken}}
X-Tenant-Subdomain: {{techstart_subdomain}}

### Expected: 200 OK with TechStart-specific statistics

### ============================================
### Validation & Error Tests
### ============================================

### 19. Try to create company without required fields
POST {{baseUrl}}/companies HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAcme.response.body.data.accessToken}}
X-Tenant-Subdomain: {{acme_subdomain}}

{
  "industry": "Technology"
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request (missing name)

### 20. Try to create duplicate company name in same tenant
POST {{baseUrl}}/companies HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAcme.response.body.data.accessToken}}
X-Tenant-Subdomain: {{acme_subdomain}}

{
  "name": "TechVision Solutions",
  "industry": "Software"
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request (company name already exists)

### 21. Try to access company without authentication
GET {{baseUrl}}/companies HTTP/1.1
X-Tenant-Subdomain: {{acme_subdomain}}

### Expected: 401 Unauthorized

### 22. Try to create company without tenant header
POST {{baseUrl}}/companies HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAcme.response.body.data.accessToken}}

{
  "name": "Test Company",
  "industry": "Technology"
}

### Expected: 401 Unauthorized (tenant required)

### ============================================
### Advanced Features Tests
### ============================================

### 23. Search companies across multiple fields
GET {{baseUrl}}/companies?search=tech HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAcme.response.body.data.accessToken}}
X-Tenant-Subdomain: {{acme_subdomain}}

### Expected: 200 OK with companies matching "tech" in name, industry, website, or email

### 24. Filter by owner (get companies owned by current user)
GET {{baseUrl}}/companies?ownerId={{loginAcme.response.body.data.user.id}} HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAcme.response.body.data.accessToken}}
X-Tenant-Subdomain: {{acme_subdomain}}

### Expected: 200 OK with companies owned by John

### ============================================
### Cleanup: Delete Companies
### ============================================

### 25. Delete the test company
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/companies/{{createCompany1.response.body.data.id}} HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAcme.response.body.data.accessToken}}
X-Tenant-Subdomain: {{acme_subdomain}}

### Expected: 200 OK (company deleted)

### 26. Verify company is deleted
GET {{baseUrl}}/companies/{{createCompany1.response.body.data.id}} HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAcme.response.body.data.accessToken}}
X-Tenant-Subdomain: {{acme_subdomain}}

### Expected: 404 Not Found

### 27. Try to delete company from wrong tenant
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/companies/{{createCompanyTechStart.response.body.data.id}} HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAcme.response.body.data.accessToken}}
X-Tenant-Subdomain: {{acme_subdomain}}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request or 404 Not Found (tenant isolation)

### ============================================
### Summary:
### ✓ Full CRUD operations
### ✓ Pagination and filtering
### ✓ Search functionality (name, industry, website, email)
### ✓ Filter by industry, owner, tags
### ✓ Sort by any field
### ✓ Tenant isolation enforced
### ✓ Validation working
### ✓ Statistics endpoint with revenue aggregation
### ============================================
